y.\n\n4. **All-in (-2)**: Extremely risky and -EV. I'm likely behind and have minimal equity.\n\n**Reason:**\nChecking is the optimal play here. I have position (acting after seeing opponent's check), a weak draw (only 4 outs for ~9% equity), and no made hand. Checking allows me to:\n- See the river for free\n- Avoid committing more chips with poor equity\n- Maintain pot control\n- Potentially bluff or value-bet on the river if I improve or read weakness\n\nGiven that my opponent checked the turn after betting the flop, they might be slowing down with a marginal hand, a missed draw, or setting a trap. Checking back is prudent risk management.\n\n**Answer:** 0"}
