ity\n\nGiven the pot is likely small (just blinds so far with checks), a raise of about 200 chips represents a reasonable bet to take control.\n\nReason: I have a weak made hand (pair of 6s) against an opponent showing weakness through checks. A small raise applies pressure and gathers information while not overcommitting chips. Checking risks giving free cards to flush draws or overcards. This raise size allows me to fold if faced with resistance while potentially taking down the pot against weak holdings or draws.\n\nAnswer: 200"}
